spec.org describes what the skill must do, but Claude needs concrete
steps to carry it out in lab-claude, which has no ports tree and no
root.

The tree is a blobless git clone so the first run stays small while
the port history used for changelogs and conventions remains
reachable. make runs with its distfiles, work directory, and options
database under /var/tmp, since the defaults are root-owned and the
port would otherwise fail in the config step before fetching. The
patch is made with plain git format-patch because it is applied with
git am to a ports tree, where lab's change ids mean nothing.

The commit conventions are the ones oss/freebsd-ports/CLAUDE.md
reviews against, less the PR: trailer, which cannot exist before
Pat files the bug.
